=== PARITY (web source read end-to-end; every t() + branch reproduced) ===
  - Data sources: the web `<label>` has NO data hook — its only hook is
    `useTranslation`. There is therefore no P1/S8 state-holder to bind and NO HTTP in
    the view (vacuously satisfied). The acceptance "hooks bind to the state-holder
    layer" maps to: the sole i18n dependency is resolved via the P1/S10 catalog.
  - Composition (web `<label>` + children + danger `*` span + VisuallyHidden):
      * label text -> Text(LocalizedStringKey) | Text(verbatim:) at Font.TS.label /
        Color.TS.textSecondary (matches the native TSLabel typography role).
      * required `*` -> Text("*") at Color.TS.statusDanger (web `text-rose-300`),
        `.accessibilityHidden(true)` == web `aria-hidden="true"`.
      * VisuallyHidden "required" -> the element's `.accessibilityLabel` appends the
        localized word so the combined accessible name is "<label> required"
        (web appends `<VisuallyHidden>{` ${t('form.required')}`}</VisuallyHidden>`).
        Realized with `.accessibilityElement(children:.ignore)` + `.accessibilityLabel`.
  - States (ALL real branches render; each has a #if DEBUG preview + a unit test):
      required == false  -> bare label.
      required == true   -> label + danger `*` + accessible "<label> required".
      The generic surface-template states loading / empty / error / stale / offline do
      NOT exist in the web source (no data source). They are deliberately NOT
      fabricated for a purely presentational label (Honesty covenant #2/#3) — inventing
      async states absent from the spec would be drift, not parity. Both genuine
      branches are previewed (5 previews) and unit-tested.
  - i18n (P1/S10): the ONE web key `form.required` is preserved — catalog key
    `translation.form.required` (en "required", state=translated) EXISTS and is the
    only `translation.*` literal referenced by the shipped code. No English literals:
    the only Text(...) calls are the catalog key, the `*` glyph (Text(verbatim:"*")),
    and caller-provided runtime labels (Text(verbatim: value), parity with web children).
  - Accessibility: the required field's VoiceOver name reads "<label> required" (the
    localized word, never the `*` glyph); `*` is hidden; Dynamic Type via Font.TS;
    reduce-motion N/A (no animation). Adapter rule unit-tested across 5 edges.
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): TSFormLabelDiagnostics.reportViewOpened emits `view.opened`
    with surface slug "Label" (OSLog default sink; the `*` redaction-safe contract
    mirrors OSLogDashboardWidgetTelemetry). Opt-in (nil default) so ordinary inline
    label use stays silent; a host injects the shared sink. Emission unit-tested.

